Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 09:57:58 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] ZoneRebalance: the definitions as equations; the anchor
 contract specializes Contract.zero

zoneRowPre_iff, zoneRebalanceIndex_eq, zoneRebalanceIndex_le, and the fields of the data maps and
the endpoints (simps, without the simp attribute). The private zr_anchorContract, the same
construction as Contract.zero, now specializes it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../TuringMachine/Build/ZoneRebalance.lean    | 55 ++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 41 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)

diff --git a/TCSlib/Complexity/TuringMachine/Build/ZoneRebalance.lean b/TCSlib/Complexity/TuringMachine/Build/ZoneRebalance.lean
index 9e687b16..ca48d3af 100644
--- a/TCSlib/Complexity/TuringMachine/Build/ZoneRebalance.lean
+++ b/TCSlib/Complexity/TuringMachine/Build/ZoneRebalance.lean
@@ -57,6 +57,10 @@ mirror). The amortization `Σ_i T/2^{i-1} · 2^i = O(T log T)` is the consumer's
 * `Turing.zoneRebalancePost_state_done`, `Turing.zoneRebalanceData_of_short`,
   `Turing.zoneRebalanceIndex_extend_of_short`: the two exits.
 * `Turing.zoneRebalancePost_frames`, `Turing.zoneExtendPost_frames`: the footprints.
+* `Turing.zoneRowPre_iff`, `Turing.zoneRebalanceIndex_eq`, `Turing.zoneRebalanceIndex_le`,
+  and the fields of `Turing.zoneRebalanceData`, `Turing.zoneExtendData`,
+  `Turing.zoneRebalancePost` and `Turing.zoneExtendPost` (`Turing.zoneRebalancePost_state` and
+  the rest): the definitions as equations.
 
 ## References
 
@@ -125,6 +129,30 @@ def zoneRowHi {k : ℕ} {S : Type} {x : List (ZoneSym k)} (r : ZoneData k → 
     (D : ZoneData k) (d : Cfg 2 (ZoneSym k) S x) (j : Fin 2) : ℤ :=
   if j = 0 then (zoneStart (r D + 1) : ℤ) else d.workTapePos j + C * (2 ^ r D + 1)
 
+/-! The definitions above as equations, without the `simp` attribute, so that consumers never
+unfold them: the data maps' and the endpoints' fields (generated by `simps`), the
+precondition's and the scanned index's bodies. -/
+
+attribute [simps (config := { isSimp := false })] zoneRebalanceData zoneExtendData
+  zoneRebalancePost zoneExtendPost
+
+/-- `Turing.zoneRowPre`'s defining equation. -/
+theorem zoneRowPre_iff {k : ℕ} {S : Type} {x : List (ZoneSym k)} (D : ZoneData k)
+    (d : Cfg 2 (ZoneSym k) S x) :
+    zoneRowPre D d ↔
+      d.workTapes 0 = zonedTape D.2 ∧ d.workTapePos 0 = 0 ∧ ∀ q, d.workTapes 1 q = none :=
+  Iff.rfl
+
+/-- `Turing.zoneRebalanceIndex`'s defining equation. -/
+theorem zoneRebalanceIndex_eq {k : ℕ} (dir : Bool) (t : Fin k) (D : ZoneData k) :
+    zoneRebalanceIndex dir t D = zoneShiftIndex dir (D.2 t) :=
+  rfl
+
+/-- The scanned index is at most the level count (`Turing.zoneShiftIndex_le`). -/
+theorem zoneRebalanceIndex_le {k : ℕ} (dir : Bool) (t : Fin k) (D : ZoneData k) :
+    zoneRebalanceIndex dir t D ≤ D.1 :=
+  zoneShiftIndex_le dir (D.2 t)
+
 /-- Restate a contract's exit set by an equality, without changing any of its fields.
 
 **Proof sketch.** Re-wrap its segment and exit membership through the set equality. -/
@@ -1566,15 +1594,12 @@ private def zr_loopBack : SeekPhase ⊕ (Option Bool ⊕ Option Bool) → Option
 private abbrev zr_loopTM (k : ℕ) : MultiTapeTM 2 (ZoneSym k) (Σ b, zr_loopPh b) :=
   zr_hostTM (zr_loopBodyTM k) (Sum.inl .run) zr_loopBack
 
-/-- The anchor phase's stationary leaf as a zero-time contract at the anchor. -/
-private def zr_anchorContract {k : ℕ} (x : List (ZoneSym k)) :
+/-- The anchor phase's stationary leaf: the zero-time contract at the anchor
+(`Turing.Contract.zero`). -/
+private abbrev zr_anchorContract {k : ℕ} (x : List (ZoneSym k)) :
     Contract (zr_cellTM (k := k) 0 (fun _ => false) none 0) (some false) {some (some false)}
       Unit x :=
-  Contract.ofSegment (fun _ _ => True) (fun _ _ => 0) (fun _ d => d)
-    (fun _ d => d.workTapePos) (fun _ d => d.workTapePos)
-    (fun _ d _ _ => Segment.zero
-      ((headBox_iff _ _ _).mpr fun _ => Finset.mem_Icc.mpr ⟨le_rfl, le_rfl⟩))
-    (fun _ d hd _ => by rw [hd]; exact Set.mem_singleton _)
+  Contract.zero _ (some false) Unit x
 
